      "body": "## Summary\n\n`get_tokenizer(..., revision=<sha>)` loaded the tokenizer at that pin, then ran the post-load fixes with `tokenizer_revision=None`. The fixes looked up `tokenizer.json` / `tokenizer_config.json` at the default revision and bailed out when the cache had only the pinned snapshot.\n\nThe pin is now `tokenizer_revision` when that argument is set, otherwise the `revision` keyword. An explicit `tokenizer_revision` still wins.\n\nFixes #47125\n\n## Test\n\n`python3 -m pytest test/registered/unit/tokenizer/test_post_load_revision.py -q`\n\nThe post-load revision was `None` for `revision=\"abc123\"` before this change and `abc123` after it. No Hub download.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40762956030](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40762956030)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40762955866](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40762955866)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40762955818](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40762955818)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
